feat(research): add VECTOR profitability research packages and Go candidate engine

Implements the VECTOR v1.1 research stack on top of the existing paper trading core.

- P-1 slippage attribution, P-2 risk and capital efficiency, P-4 cost structure
  with observed MFE/MAE, P-5 concentration and dependence, P-6 decision gate and
  the A0-A3 paper-only autonomy stack as read-only research services with
  append-only records, idempotent generations and fail-closed gates.
- Go research engine: five versioned candidate cohorts with mechanical
  look-ahead controls (causal mutation test, future-only negative control, higher
  timeframe candle closure), a local archive loader and a realistic dataset
  benchmark that writes CPU and heap pprof profiles.
- Go engine optimisation iteration 2: the exact rational RSI hot path is replaced
  by exact integer arithmetic in the internal scale 24. The golden fixture
  70.46413502, the locked backtest golden hash, the trade counts and the net PnL
  are unchanged, while the synthetic 10,000 candle backtest drops from 241-275 ms
  to 101-119 ms and the realistic BTCUSDT 5m backtest from 78.7 ms to 37.0 ms.
- Backtest engine fix for the missing opened_at key on open and partially closed
  positions, with regression coverage for no trades, partial exits and boundary
  ranges.
- Read-only research API and the Profitability Research UI page.

Paper-only by construction: no order path, no exchange trade credentials, no
change to the eight primary paper accounts, no promotion applied, all autonomy
feature flags remain OFF.
EOF
