## 3. Close prior P-1 correctness and implement PROFIT-1 P-2

- Check actual status of P-1 and G1. Verify reference-price reconstruction assumes adverse-only simulator slippage and cannot represent favorable real fills. Preserve `RECORDED_SIMULATOR_ADVERSE_RECONSTRUCTED` or compatible accurately documented provenance.
- **Critical partial-close issue:** The historical 29-position/65-execution fixture contains one `PARTIALLY_CLOSED` position with entry quantity 0.021 and exited quantity 0.010, leaving 0.011 open. The entire entry slippage of 0.021 cannot automatically be added to **realized** lifecycle net PnL from exited quantity 0.010. Verify matching execution IDs, cutoffs and PnL populations; allocate entry slippage proportionally to realized vs open inventory according to verified ledger conventions. Keep total full-fill execution slippage separate from realized-only counterfactual. If matching is inconclusive, mark hypothetical net `NOT_VERIFIED`, rather than forcing 72.6789 USDT. Add negative controls.
- Implement P-2 **exactly per PROFIT-1 Rev 2.1 sections 6, 8 and 18**, reusing existing `QuantPortfolioMetricsService`, `PerformanceStatisticsService`, `DailyPerformanceService`, P-1 service and ledger reconciliation. Do not rebuild V5.3 accounting.
- Deliver position-level net R, mean/median R; cost-to-risk using matched-scope P-1 data; net profit factor, net win rate and payoff; drawdown using valid initial high-water mark and timestamped equity, time underwater; bounded carry-forward TWAE with uncovered gaps; turnover; daily returns and daily realized net R; dependence-aware ESS per normative method; source-backed risk-capital/notional/exposure measurements; margin only where directly recorded (else `NULL`/`NOT_RECORDED_IN_LEDGER`).
- Source cutoff and `known_at` constraints. Handle partial exits, unclosed positions, missing risk capital, zero denominators, signed funding and external flows explicitly. 20 non-overlapping valid days and ESS >=20 are **minimum data sufficiency gates**, not proof of positive expectancy. Honor stricter existing policy.
- Use append-only immutable research generations, valid idempotency payload hashes, heartbeat/stale-job/retry semantics, performance-bounded separate research queue and no ledger writes. Test migration only on isolated test DB. No synchronous long-running HTTP computations.
- Complete the specified API and Russian Quasar UI and create `reports/profit-growth/03-p2-risk-and-capital-efficiency.md` and `reports/profit-growth/P2_evidence.json` with genuine raw evidence and limitations.

## 4. Implement PROFIT-1 P-5 (separate verified change set)

After P-2 is accepted locally, implement **section 10 / relevant §18** exactly:
- Inclusive/exclusive time-interval semantics as specified; analyze same-side overlaps and **opposite-side overlaps as a bipartite graph**. Never infer nonexistent pairwise edges from connected components.
- Detect concentration of net outcome in individual positions, days, symbols, directions, regimes and overlapping market episodes. Audit any duplicated or transitive counting.
- Synchronize equity time series only where timestamps/data coverage support it; do not silently forward-fill unlimited gaps. Use source-backed samples, proper status and ESS where applicable.
- Full reproducibility, independent eight-account reporting, read-only APIs/UI, golden and negative controls, PostgreSQL integration, evidence manifest/report.
- Do NOT combine the eight primary paper ledgers or mistake overlapping observations for independent samples.

## 5. Implement PROFIT-1 P-4 (separate verified change set)

After accepted P-1 and required upstream dependencies, implement **section 9 / relevant §18**:
